P-12 (spec 017, the night shift; T090 round 2): tools/gates/compose_policy.py allows one named local base.

What it changes:
  - LOCAL_BASES names the (file, build argument) pairs whose FROM may be a bare ${ARG} with no default: today one,
    deploy/night-shift/images/worker.Dockerfile's TOOLCHAIN_IMAGE. That image is the devcontainer image the night
    shift's install builds first from .devcontainer/Dockerfile, whose own FROMs this policy checks, so no registry
    can pin it. The worker's other base (docker-cli) and the studio's, comfyui's, and egress's take their defaults
    from deploy/images.lock lines on the branch, so the policy checks them as it checks every other Dockerfile.
  - Any other argument, the same argument in any other file, a FROM that adds to the argument (${TOOLCHAIN_IMAGE}-x),
    or a default given to it, is checked as before.
  - tools/gates/test/test_compose_policy.py: two tests (the pair passes only at its own file and argument; a default
    is held to the lock).

Why: R3, the install's make check in a night container, failed policy on the four night-shift Dockerfiles
(FROM ${ARG} without a default). Three are fixed on the branch; this is the fourth. Until it merges, the branch's
make check and the gate's policy step FAIL on that one line, and R3 names it as known (P-12). So apply it on main
before feat/017-the-night-shift's gate.

Apply from the repository's top: patch -p1 < docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p12.patch
--- a/tools/gates/compose_policy.py
+++ b/tools/gates/compose_policy.py
@@ -74,6 +74,13 @@
